# Trivy ignore list.
# Format: one line per ignored vulnerability.
#   <vuln-id>  <expiry-date>  <reason>
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-12345  2026-12-31  "dev-only dep, fix tracked in JIRA-123"
#
# The expiry date forces a re-review. After the expiry, the
# ignore is removed and the vulnerability will fail the build
# again. This is the "no forever-ignores" rule.
#
# All entries must have a written reason.
# Documentation: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/v0.58/docs/scanner/vulnerability/#how-to-ignore-vulnerabilities

# Deno-specific vulnerability in esbuild; not exploitable in Node.js.
# Transitive dep of Sanity v4 studio; fix blocked on Sanity v6 upgrade.
GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr  2026-12-31  "Deno-only vuln, Sanity ecosystem transitive dep"

# DOM Clobbering in prismjs; transitive dep of @sanity/assist.
# Fix blocked on @sanity/assist v6 upgrade.
CVE-2024-53382  2026-12-31  "prismjs transitive dep of @sanity/assist"

# DoS via js-yaml merge key handling; transitive dep of Sanity v4.
# Fix blocked on Sanity v6 upgrade.
CVE-2026-53550  2026-12-31  "js-yaml transitive dep of Sanity ecosystem"
